<title>USA: Ampco-Pittsburg stake cut by Gabelli group.</title>
<headline>Ampco-Pittsburg stake cut by Gabelli group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investor Mario Gabelli said it cut its stake in Ampco-Pittsburg Corp to 1,799,700 shares, or 18.79 percent. In March its stake was 19.86 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions included a net 19,000 shares sold between September 16 and November 8 at prices ranging from $11.6250 and $12.9625 per share.</p>
</text>
